  "text": "Imagine you are looking for a specific word in a massive, unindexed dictionary. Without an index, you would have to start at page one and read every single entry until you found the word you wanted. This is analogous to a **table scan** (or full table scan) in database terms. When a query like `SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = 'alice@example.com'` runs without an index, the database engine must sequentially read every row in the `users` table to find Alice\u2019s record. If the table contains ten million rows, the database performs ten million I/O operations, which is slow and resource-intensive.\n\n",
